      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(agents): resolve channel and account messagePrefix overrides",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`resolveMessagePrefix` only read global `messages.messagePrefix` (or an\nexplicit caller `configured` override). Channel-level and account-level\n`messagePrefix` fields (supported in channel schemas such as WhatsApp\nand Zalouser) were ignored, while `resolveResponsePrefix` already\ncascades account → channel → global. Operators who set per-channel or\nper-account inbound prefixes got the wrong prefix or identity default.\n\n## Evidence\n\n```console\n$ pnpm exec vitest run src/agents/identity.per-channel-prefix.test.ts\n✓ resolveMessagePrefix with per-channel override (6)\n✓ 29 tests passed\n\n$ pnpm exec tsx -e '...'  # channel-aware resolveMessagePrefix\nglobal [Global]\nchannel [WA]\naccount [Biz]\neffective [WA]\n```\n\nRed-green: without the production change, the new channel/account tests\nfail (expected global); with the fix, all 29 tests pass.\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\n- **Behavior or issue addressed:** channel/account `messagePrefix` overrides ignored\n- **Real environment tested:** macOS, Node via worktree on branch fix/message-prefix-channel-account\n- **Exact steps or command run after this patch:** `pnpm exec vitest run src/agents/identity.per-channel-prefix.test.ts` and `pnpm exec tsx` calling `resolveMessagePrefix` with channel/account opts\n- **Evidence after fix:** terminal output above (channel and account prefixes win over global)\n- **Observed result after fix:** account `[Biz]`, channel `[WA]`, global `[Global]` as designed\n- **What was not tested:** live WhatsApp inbound session with multi-account config\n\n## Summary\n\n- Cascade account → channel → global for `messagePrefix` (mirror `responsePrefix`)\n- Pass channel/account through `resolveEffectiveMessagesConfig`\n- Regression tests in `identity.per-channel-prefix.test.ts`\n\nCloses #102937\n",
        "branch": "fix/message-prefix-channel-account",
